## Source audit and change

- Added `MessageExtSubtype` getter/setter hooks for Java virtual born/store
  timestamps, born host, sysFlag, body CRC, commit-log offset, store size and
  prepared-transaction offset.
- Routed the corresponding `MessageExt` accessors through those hooks with
  stored-value fallback. Born-host string/name/bytes and store-host bytes
  helpers continue to read the stored fields because the pinned Java
  implementations do so directly; the virtual born/store host getters remain
  independently dispatched.
- Extended the invoked Java custom subtype with distinct metadata getters and
  eight counted setters. Host overrides return `127.0.0.1:10913`, while their
  setters store `127.0.0.1:10912` / `127.0.0.1:10911` in the base fields. The
  fixture compares both virtual getter values and field-derived string/name/
  IPv4-byte helper results.
- Updated the Phase 6, Phase 10, Phase 18 and release checklist records.

## Verification

- PASS: pinned Java runtime fixture regeneration; 9 Running Info,
  27 direct-consume and 15 reset cases.
- PASS: focused `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --test
  runtime_direct_consume` (3 tests).
- PASS: `cargo test --workspace --locked --quiet` and
  `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked --quiet`.
- PASS: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`.
- PASS: `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`; 37 scenarios,
  runtime direct-consumer fixture, fixture drift checks, 83 typed headers,
  16 typed bodies and Java/Rust cross-decodes. Existing JDK Unsafe and
  reflective-final-field warnings were emitted.
- An initial fixture attempt called Java host-bytes helpers with subtype host
  overrides whose setters did not populate the base host fields. The pinned
  helpers threw in that case because they read the fields directly. The fixture
  now uses overrides that call `super` for field storage, while differing
  virtual getter values; Rust mirrors the resulting split, and the final
  fixture/tests above pass.

